{"In Delete method, klog.NewContext passes the base logger d.Log instead of the enriched log variable that includes name/kind/method fields, so downstream code extracting the logger from context will lack structured context": 0.9715380072593689, "In Create method, when d.Storage.Create fails, d.recordLegacyDuration is called instead of d.recordStorageDuration, recording storage failure latency under the wrong metric histogram": 0.9938294291496277, "In Delete method, the success-path metric call passes the object name instead of options.Kind as the metric label, creating unbounded high-cardinality metrics that can exhaust monitoring system memory": 0.969972550868988, "In Update method, when d.Storage.Update fails, d.recordLegacyDuration is called instead of d.recordStorageDuration, recording storage failure latency under the wrong metric histogram": 0.995039165019989, "In DeleteCollection's async goroutine, the legacy operation's duration is recorded via d.recordStorageDuration instead of d.recordLegacyDuration, attributing legacy write latency to the storage metric histogram": 0.9988056421279907, "The request context is passed directly to asynchronous goroutines, so when the HTTP request completes, the parent context is cancelled, which immediately aborts the async legacy writes before they can complete": 0.8998710513114929}